From: Jean Iaquinta <jeani@uio.no>
Subject: [PATCH] ch4/ofi: fix AM header lost when a pipelined send is issued deferred

MPIDI_OFI_do_am_isend_pipeline() computed send_req->am_data using the
am_hdr_sz *parameter*, which progress passes as 0 for deferred issues
(documented as ignored; the valid value lives in the sreq header). When a
pipelined first segment (offset == 0) had been queued before any segment
was sent (deferred queue non-empty at call time), MPIDI_OFI_am_isend_pipeline()
copied the real AM header into the pack buffer and then packed the payload
at am_data = header + 0, overwriting the header. The target then parsed
payload bytes as the MPIDIG message header (e.g. win_id = 0x61616161...),
MPIDIU_map_lookup() returned MPIDIU_MAP_NOT_FOUND, and dereferencing it
as MPIR_Win crashed (SIGSEGV reading win->base at 0x47). Reproducible with
osu_put_bw/osu_get_bw and large pipelined point-to-point messages once a
second large AM op is issued while a previous pipeline is still queued.
Use MPIDI_OFI_AM_SREQ_HDR(sreq, am_hdr_sz), consistent with
MPIDI_OFI_am_isend_pipeline(), which already sizes the header from the sreq.

Same defect as fixed for mpich 5.0.2 (j34ni/alpine-apk commit edc0ca8);
root-caused under ASan on a 2-container TCP repro (no RDMA hardware
involved). Upstream status: bug still present in main (verified
2026-10-01, no known upstream fix).

---
--- mpich-4.3.2/src/mpid/ch4/netmod/ofi/ofi_am_impl.h	2026-10-01 19:46:47.957544755 +0000
+++ mpich-4.3.2/src/mpid/ch4/netmod/ofi/ofi_am_impl.h	2026-10-01 19:46:47.976736319 +0000
@@ -677,7 +677,9 @@
         send_req->msg_hdr = pack_buffer;
         send_req->am_hdr = (char *) pack_buffer + sizeof(MPIDI_OFI_am_header_t);
         if (offset == 0) {
-            send_req->am_data = (char *) send_req->am_hdr + am_hdr_sz;
+            /* am_hdr_sz parameter is ignored when issue_deferred is true; the valid
+             * size is the one saved in the sreq header (see am_init_sreq). */
+            send_req->am_data = (char *) send_req->am_hdr + MPIDI_OFI_AM_SREQ_HDR(sreq, am_hdr_sz);
         } else {
             send_req->am_data = (char *) send_req->am_hdr;
         }
